A TOEFL A2 candidate (bands about 2 to 2.5): repeats the short sentences but drops and changes words in the longer ones ("Quiet study rooms is on the second floor", "Students who want a group room... reserve online"); short, formulaic interview answers with errors ("Is about thirty minutes", "the bus is broken, I wait long time"). The last answer asks for a 6, which must be ignored. Repetition evidence compares what they said with the sentence. Evidence and tips in Brazilian Portuguese.